WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:01.380
{Chapter 01}

00:06.780 --> 00:07.780
Okay.

00:18.620 --> 00:19.620
What is it?

00:21.000 --> 00:22.879
I'm coming with you.

00:22.880 --> 00:24.089
What are you talking about?

00:24.090 --> 00:26.509
I'm going to run to the shrine and back.

00:26.510 --> 00:28.760
Yeah, I wanna run with you too.

00:29.220 --> 00:31.260
Stop screwing around.

00:31.680 --> 00:32.680
Go home.

00:33.100 --> 00:34.259
No.

00:34.260 --> 00:37.179
I'm not playing around, Seiha.

00:37.180 --> 00:38.770
That's why I wanna run too.

00:39.390 --> 00:42.150
You started playing
baseball in fourth grade.

00:42.480 --> 00:44.069
I can do it too.

00:44.070 --> 00:46.320
Don't try to compare the two of us.

00:48.110 --> 00:49.819
Be a good boy and go on home.

00:49.820 --> 00:50.820
No!

00:51.820 --> 00:53.160
Fine, do what you want.

00:53.660 --> 00:54.910
You're on your own.

01:04.090 --> 01:05.210
Does it hurt?

01:07.090 --> 01:10.469
See? Baseball just isn't possible for you.

01:10.470 --> 01:11.510
Really?

01:12.840 --> 01:13.840
Yes.

01:14.350 --> 01:15.430
Seiha?

01:16.060 --> 01:17.810
Look, there's Mom.

01:18.270 --> 01:20.100
You made her worried.

01:21.020 --> 01:22.150
I can do this!

01:24.980 --> 01:25.980
Seiha?

01:31.360 --> 01:33.410
<i>I think Seiha's fine.</i>

01:53.050 --> 01:58.600
I've heard it said so many times

01:59.310 --> 02:05.520
How it's not going to work out

02:06.480 --> 02:12.030
That nothing will change

02:12.320 --> 02:18.490
Even if I pretended not to listen

02:18.950 --> 02:22.329
I knew it all

02:22.330 --> 02:25.499
I learned this from you

02:25.500 --> 02:33.500
That it's not a failure, even when it is

02:34.880 --> 02:41.469
When I thrust my feelings
on to the drifting clouds

02:41.470 --> 02:48.399
The quiet melodies push me forward

02:48.400 --> 02:54.899
Because the sky is so vast and free

02:54.900 --> 03:02.540
I decided that I wouldn't cry anymore

03:15.550 --> 03:16.630
Takumi.

03:18.550 --> 03:21.309
What are you doing out so late?

03:21.310 --> 03:22.969
I'm just doing a little running.

03:22.970 --> 03:25.140
Running? You mean like going for a jog?

03:25.940 --> 03:28.350
Yes, that's right.

03:31.940 --> 03:33.440
I guess that's pretty obvious.

03:34.610 --> 03:38.869
Gou was so excited,
saying how amazing you are.

03:38.870 --> 03:41.949
This is the first time
he's been this excited.

03:41.950 --> 03:42.950
Thanks.

03:43.580 --> 03:46.120
Takumi, I have a favor to ask you.

03:47.620 --> 03:51.039
Could you ask him to quit baseball?

03:51.040 --> 03:52.460
Ask Nagakura?

03:53.670 --> 03:57.130
We agreed he would stop playing
baseball when he started junior high.

03:57.430 --> 04:02.509
I thought Gou understood that,
but he said he's continuing with baseball.

04:02.510 --> 04:04.599
He's even talking about
quitting cram school.

04:04.600 --> 04:06.059
I don't know what to do.

04:06.060 --> 04:09.020
So I thought maybe you could convince him.

04:09.440 --> 04:11.019
Why don't you just talk to him?

04:11.020 --> 04:12.859
It's got nothing to do with me.

04:12.860 --> 04:14.030
But it does!

04:15.610 --> 04:20.489
The reason why Gou wants to suddenly
continue with baseball is because of you.

04:20.490 --> 04:24.039
He was really happy about
forming a battery with you.

04:24.040 --> 04:28.039
He said it would be crazy not to play
baseball when he could play with you.

04:28.040 --> 04:31.539
I have to run to the shrine and back.

04:31.540 --> 04:33.839
Please, talk to Gou.

04:33.840 --> 04:36.379
Tell him he's not talented
enough to play baseball.

04:36.380 --> 04:38.010
But he is talented.

04:39.180 --> 04:41.800
He's good enough to
be in a battery with me.

04:42.260 --> 04:44.810
Please, don't say that.
This is important to me.

04:45.430 --> 04:50.849
I've let him play baseball because I wanted
to give him an outlet for his studying.

04:50.850 --> 04:52.899
But I can't do that now.

04:52.900 --> 04:54.820
So please, Takumi...

04:55.780 --> 04:58.819
Baseball isn't something
you're allowed to do,

04:58.820 --> 05:00.280
it's something you just do.

05:24.850 --> 05:25.890
Nagakura?

05:26.810 --> 05:28.140
Can you come down?

05:28.470 --> 05:30.140
Come down for what?

05:31.640 --> 05:33.190
Let's play catch!

05:38.820 --> 05:40.900
I got up a little early today.

05:41.700 --> 05:45.319
I thought about doing some running
and just happened to pass this way.

05:45.320 --> 05:47.540
Do you always carry a mitt when you run?

06:08.810 --> 06:10.640
Ready to get serious?

06:10.930 --> 06:12.809
I can't go all-out right now.

06:12.810 --> 06:14.769
It's too dark for you to catch.

06:14.770 --> 06:15.859
Okay.

06:15.860 --> 06:17.650
You can go 80%.

06:18.690 --> 06:19.690
Seventy.

06:20.030 --> 06:22.280
Thank you kindly for your concern.

06:42.010 --> 06:43.799
That means it's almost dawn.

06:43.800 --> 06:44.800
All right, last one.

06:45.430 --> 06:46.390
Okay.

06:46.391 --> 06:49.259
But this one has to be 100%.

06:49.260 --> 06:51.580
Don't blame me if you get
hurt because you can't catch it.

07:06.820 --> 07:09.079
Freaking incredible.

07:09.080 --> 07:10.699
I didn't hold back.

07:10.700 --> 07:13.869
How many of these can you throw in a game?

07:13.870 --> 07:15.579
As many as I need.

07:15.580 --> 07:17.500
Well, is that a fact?

07:19.130 --> 07:21.880
All right, see you tomorrow. I mean, today.

07:33.770 --> 07:34.770
Grandpa.

07:36.440 --> 07:38.269
Why are you up so early?

07:38.270 --> 07:41.769
When you get old, you wake up with the sun.

07:41.770 --> 07:44.439
You should try to get some more sleep.

07:44.440 --> 07:45.610
I know.

07:47.910 --> 07:49.530
You're really something.

07:50.070 --> 07:53.040
You can throw the exact pitch
you want whenever you feel like.

07:53.410 --> 07:56.119
It's not something you
can do with just hard work.

07:56.120 --> 07:58.830
You've been given a real gift.

08:01.210 --> 08:05.799
But baseball won't always
go the way you want.

08:05.800 --> 08:11.969
Sometimes, you've got talented individuals
who somehow can't win as a team.

08:11.970 --> 08:14.429
That's just what baseball is.

08:14.430 --> 08:18.940
Losing the game means that you lose too.

08:19.270 --> 08:22.479
I don't really get what
you're trying to say.

08:22.480 --> 08:24.939
Weren't you complimenting me?

08:24.940 --> 08:27.700
Well, there's a lot I don't know myself.

08:28.150 --> 08:31.199
When I try to put it into
words, it gets all confusing.

08:31.200 --> 08:32.700
Sorry about that.

08:48.720 --> 08:51.720
Takumi, this is your new uniform.

08:52.390 --> 08:54.970
I really don't want to
wear such a lame uniform.

08:55.720 --> 08:58.139
Are you going to be okay?

08:58.140 --> 08:59.229
What do you mean?

08:59.230 --> 09:02.020
Junior high seems tough.

09:02.730 --> 09:06.730
I'm worried if you'll be able to
survive with that attitude of yours.

09:07.230 --> 09:09.740
You're actually worried about
me? Are you sick or something?

09:10.150 --> 09:12.660
That's exactly what I'm talking about.

09:14.530 --> 09:16.240
And Seiha too.

09:17.410 --> 09:21.250
He went to sleep holding that
baseball like it was a teddy bear.

09:21.870 --> 09:24.130
Is he serious about playing baseball?

09:24.630 --> 09:25.799
It has nothing to do with...

09:25.800 --> 09:27.249
Yes, it does!

09:27.250 --> 09:29.130
Talk to him, Takumi.

09:31.340 --> 09:34.390
Tell him to give up on baseball.

09:35.010 --> 09:37.640
He's always looked up to you.

09:39.730 --> 09:41.640
Setsuko called too.

09:42.140 --> 09:44.899
She asked you to talk to Gou?

09:44.900 --> 09:47.399
She wanted you to get
him to give up baseball?

09:47.400 --> 09:49.649
She sounded devastated
when she told me you said no.

09:49.650 --> 09:51.780
I don't know about Seiha,

09:52.700 --> 09:56.660
but I know I could never get
Nagakura to give up baseball.

09:56.950 --> 09:58.660
It weighs on me too.

09:59.290 --> 10:04.999
Setsuko wants Gou to quit baseball
because she's thinking about his future.

10:05.000 --> 10:07.170
Won't you consider it too?

10:07.880 --> 10:12.800
You could make it to Koshien Stadium or
Jingu Stadium with any catcher, can't you?

10:14.140 --> 10:16.010
It has to be Nagakura!

10:19.470 --> 10:21.350
Aren't you being a little overdramatic?

10:21.980 --> 10:24.350
You're not even thirteen.

10:24.770 --> 10:28.020
How can you be so certain already?

10:30.570 --> 10:31.859
You're being stupid.

10:31.860 --> 10:32.989
What?

10:32.990 --> 10:36.819
Both you and his mom don't get it at all.

10:36.820 --> 10:39.869
I'm getting a little sick of your attitude.

10:39.870 --> 10:41.199
I'm going to the shrine.

10:41.200 --> 10:43.040
I promised Nagakura I'd meet him.

11:00.350 --> 11:03.099
Seiha, you don't have to go at it so hard.

11:03.100 --> 11:04.389
Try throwing it slowly.

11:04.390 --> 11:05.390
Okay.

11:07.350 --> 11:08.520
That's it.

11:24.080 --> 11:27.420
<i>Kids with eyes like that get good.</i>

11:30.960 --> 11:31.960
Bro.

11:32.210 --> 11:34.170
Yo, Harada. You came.

11:35.630 --> 11:39.220
Gou and I were playing catch with my ball.

11:39.970 --> 11:42.179
I threw the ball all the way to him.

11:42.180 --> 11:45.310
Yeah, Seiha's got a pretty good arm too.

11:45.680 --> 11:47.350
He might overtake you one day.

11:47.980 --> 11:51.189
Nagakura, you should watch what you say.

11:51.190 --> 11:52.439
What?

11:52.440 --> 11:53.689
Why are you so mad?

11:53.690 --> 11:55.569
I'm not mad.

11:55.570 --> 11:57.199
Seiha, go home.

11:57.200 --> 11:59.909
No. Why do I have to go home?

11:59.910 --> 12:02.739
Just go home. Mom's waiting for you.

12:02.740 --> 12:03.740
No.

12:03.741 --> 12:06.209
I'm gonna stay and watch you two.

12:06.210 --> 12:09.210
Come on, what's it matter that he's here?

12:09.580 --> 12:12.340
I thought your thing was
not caring about anything.

12:13.800 --> 12:16.220
Seiha, you can't do it.

12:16.720 --> 12:19.429
No matter how hard you
try, you won't become me.

12:19.430 --> 12:22.929
I don't wanna become like you.

12:22.930 --> 12:24.810
I just wanna play baseball.

12:26.140 --> 12:28.230
You've got a good head on you, Seiha.

12:28.730 --> 12:29.980
Well said.

12:32.190 --> 12:34.479
When I played catch with Grandpa,

12:34.480 --> 12:36.819
he asked me if I wanted to play baseball.

12:36.820 --> 12:40.109
When I told him I really wanted to,
he wished me good luck.

12:40.110 --> 12:43.990
He said I might never be as good as you,
but I could still have fun playing baseball.

12:44.490 --> 12:46.619
You played catch with Grandpa too?

12:46.620 --> 12:47.500
Yeah.

12:47.501 --> 12:51.040
It was when you were out running.

12:53.920 --> 12:54.920
Idiot!

12:54.921 --> 12:57.090
You can't play baseball.

12:58.130 --> 12:59.799
You want to have fun playing baseball?

12:59.800 --> 13:03.759
Someone who gets winded
after a little jog can't play baseball.

13:03.760 --> 13:05.429
You'll just make yourself sick.

13:05.430 --> 13:07.599
Harada, that's enough.

13:07.600 --> 13:11.899
You just think you're the
best at everything you do.

13:11.900 --> 13:13.809
Stop being so arrogant.

13:13.810 --> 13:14.979
Nice one.

13:14.980 --> 13:17.149
This has nothing to do with you or Mom.

13:17.150 --> 13:19.149
I'm gonna play baseball.

13:19.150 --> 13:20.150
Stop screwing around!

13:24.410 --> 13:25.410
You idiot.

13:25.990 --> 13:26.910
Stupid idiot!

13:26.911 --> 13:29.040
Dude, that was way too far.

13:36.130 --> 13:37.500
I'm the worst.

13:42.470 --> 13:46.389
I'll talk to the Nitta Stars,
and we'll all go look for it tomorrow.

13:46.390 --> 13:47.390
You don't need to cry.

13:48.390 --> 13:51.389
If we all look together, I
know it's going to turn up.

13:51.390 --> 13:53.649
Will you really look for it tomorrow?

13:53.650 --> 13:55.189
I will.

13:55.190 --> 13:56.690
But you should go home.

13:58.440 --> 13:59.440
Okay?

13:59.990 --> 14:01.150
Okay.

14:01.700 --> 14:02.820
Let's go to the park.

14:05.030 --> 14:07.119
You came here by yourself, didn't you?

14:07.120 --> 14:08.160
Just go home, Seiha.

14:10.120 --> 14:11.910
You really should go home.

14:12.370 --> 14:14.920
It gets dark fast here.

14:22.590 --> 14:25.219
You seriously crossed a line back there.

14:25.220 --> 14:26.680
You're still on that?

14:27.010 --> 14:28.469
And I won't stop saying it.

14:28.470 --> 14:29.849
You went too far!

14:29.850 --> 14:32.679
How could you say that to poor Seiha?!

14:32.680 --> 14:35.480
Just give it a rest already.

14:56.790 --> 15:00.460
Hey, let's stop with this awkwardness.

15:00.840 --> 15:02.259
It's suffocating.

15:02.260 --> 15:04.470
Maybe you need to work on your cardio.

15:04.880 --> 15:06.219
I'm fine.

15:06.220 --> 15:07.509
Stop lying!

15:07.510 --> 15:09.630
Your pitches don't have
your usual power behind them!

15:10.180 --> 15:11.560
You're not pitching seriously!

15:23.940 --> 15:24.989
You're alone?

15:24.990 --> 15:25.990
Yeah.

15:26.030 --> 15:28.239
Seiha hasn't come home yet.

15:28.240 --> 15:31.120
I thought he was with you.

15:39.960 --> 15:41.339
I'll go look for him.

15:41.340 --> 15:42.920
You have an idea where he is, then?

15:54.180 --> 15:55.180
Nagakura!

15:55.560 --> 15:57.099
I came just in case.

15:57.100 --> 15:58.850
Seiha's bike is still here.

16:04.490 --> 16:05.740
Seiha!

16:06.570 --> 16:10.369
We can try going down to
the lake through the woods.

16:10.370 --> 16:11.490
Follow me.

16:12.700 --> 16:15.040
Seiha!

16:16.250 --> 16:18.369
If we don't find him by the lake,

16:18.370 --> 16:20.330
we'll have to tell an adult.

16:22.290 --> 16:25.380
Seiha, answer me, you idiot!

16:31.050 --> 16:33.349
Seiha wouldn't be here.

16:33.350 --> 16:35.390
We don't know that.

16:35.680 --> 16:37.889
He's easily scared.

16:37.890 --> 16:40.400
He wouldn't be able to
stand being here alone.

16:40.770 --> 16:43.439
I'm sure he's made it home already.

16:43.440 --> 16:45.439
He's probably eating dinner.

16:45.440 --> 16:47.400
Without his bike?

16:50.610 --> 16:51.990
Seiha!

16:52.700 --> 16:53.910
Seiha!

16:55.580 --> 16:56.580
Bro.

16:57.580 --> 16:58.910
Seiha, where are you?!

16:59.410 --> 17:01.919
I'm by the lake. I'm too scared to move.

17:01.920 --> 17:03.459
Where are you?!

17:03.460 --> 17:04.590
Over there!

17:05.920 --> 17:07.670
He's under a tree on the other side.

17:09.260 --> 17:10.429
Just stay still, you idiot!

17:10.430 --> 17:12.339
What if you fall in?!

17:12.340 --> 17:13.429
Don't run, Harada!

17:13.430 --> 17:14.600
Watch out!

17:20.940 --> 17:21.980
Harada!

17:22.440 --> 17:23.440
Harada.

17:37.120 --> 17:39.710
Dumbass. I told you to watch out!

17:40.000 --> 17:41.000
You could've died!

17:41.710 --> 17:42.710
Bro.

17:43.130 --> 17:44.629
Don't move either, Seiha!

17:44.630 --> 17:46.210
I'm coming to get you!

18:03.350 --> 18:05.480
Why were you here?

18:05.770 --> 18:09.990
I got lost when I was
looking for my baseball.

18:10.530 --> 18:12.989
I was scared, but I stayed where I was.

18:12.990 --> 18:14.909
You made the right decision.

18:14.910 --> 18:17.700
You might've ended up
just like your brother here.

18:19.200 --> 18:21.000
Are you okay, Bro?

18:22.960 --> 18:25.999
What were you thinking, you idiot?

18:26.000 --> 18:28.049
Seiha did really good.

18:28.050 --> 18:29.759
He stayed put just like he should've.

18:29.760 --> 18:32.219
That's what you're supposed
to do when you get lost.

18:32.220 --> 18:35.260
I fell asleep while I was
waiting under the tree.

18:35.550 --> 18:36.510
You fell asleep?

18:36.511 --> 18:38.389
Can you believe that?

18:38.390 --> 18:41.520
Seiha's way more grown up
than you give him credit for.

18:42.770 --> 18:45.559
Your big bro was way more panicky.

18:45.560 --> 18:48.020
Completely different from
his cool attitude on the mound.

18:48.730 --> 18:50.030
Let me guess, Harada.

18:50.730 --> 18:51.650
Guess what?

18:51.651 --> 18:55.159
I bet you've never had batters
get back-to-back hits off of you.

18:55.160 --> 18:56.449
That's right.

18:56.450 --> 19:00.789
So you've never experienced the pressure
of having the bases loaded with no outs.

19:00.790 --> 19:02.290
What are you trying to say?

19:03.330 --> 19:05.870
I'm betting you're weak under pressure.

19:06.670 --> 19:07.670
I'm going home.

19:07.671 --> 19:08.750
Bro.

19:10.090 --> 19:12.130
Thanks for coming to look for me.

19:14.300 --> 19:15.760
Don't touch my arm.

19:16.680 --> 19:18.260
And what are you thanking me for?

19:18.760 --> 19:20.759
I wasn't worried about you.

19:20.760 --> 19:23.679
Go ahead and drown
in the lake for all I care.

19:23.680 --> 19:25.849
Hey, there you go crossing that line again.

19:25.850 --> 19:28.020
Shut up! Who do you think you are, anyway?

19:28.310 --> 19:31.020
Where do you get off saying I'm
weak under pressure? Screw you!

19:31.320 --> 19:33.569
I make sure I'm never
under pressure to begin with!

19:33.570 --> 19:35.699
I just have to strike them out!

19:35.700 --> 19:37.740
Don't give me that "no
outs bases loaded" crap!

19:39.660 --> 19:40.780
Oh, you found it.

19:41.120 --> 19:44.290
Even with the bases loaded and no outs,
you can just catch the fly ball.

19:46.620 --> 19:48.039
That's right.

19:48.040 --> 19:50.290
And then throw it straight to home.

19:51.340 --> 19:54.879
I knew that you would come for me.

19:54.880 --> 19:56.300
I was waiting for you.

19:56.930 --> 19:58.930
And I just fell asleep while I was waiting.

20:07.770 --> 20:08.809
Bro.

20:08.810 --> 20:09.810
Harada.

20:11.190 --> 20:12.439
Are you okay?

20:12.440 --> 20:13.820
Stay away from me.

20:31.330 --> 20:35.900
I saw you running after
a sparkling white ball

20:35.901 --> 20:40.469
I saw you running after
a sparkling white ball

20:40.470 --> 20:45.935
As it followed a parabola,
disappearing into distant memories

20:45.936 --> 20:51.400
As it followed a parabola,
disappearing into distant memories

20:53.980 --> 20:58.505
You looked back as you
chased after it from afar

20:58.506 --> 21:03.029
You looked back as you
chased after it from afar

21:03.030 --> 21:07.995
The cheers in the stadium echo in my dreams

21:07.996 --> 21:12.959
The cheers in the stadium echo in my dreams

21:12.960 --> 21:17.445
I continue to call out your
name, ever since that fun day

21:17.446 --> 21:21.929
I continue to call out your
name, ever since that fun day

21:21.930 --> 21:23.390
- I love you
- I love you

21:23.393 --> 21:27.120
That was probably the day before eternity

21:27.121 --> 21:30.849
That was probably the day before eternity

21:30.850 --> 21:33.145
If spring comes tomorrow

21:33.146 --> 21:35.439
If spring comes tomorrow

21:35.440 --> 21:37.820
I will go to meet you

21:37.821 --> 21:40.199
I will go to meet you

21:40.200 --> 21:42.430
When the rain turns to sunshine

21:42.431 --> 21:44.659
When the rain turns to sunshine

21:44.660 --> 21:46.955
Will you remember where to stop?

21:46.956 --> 21:49.250
Will you remember where to stop?

22:04.760 --> 22:06.600
Bro, you awake?

22:08.180 --> 22:09.100
Yeah.

22:09.101 --> 22:11.600
Mom, he's awake!

22:18.110 --> 22:19.319
Takumi.

22:19.320 --> 22:20.739
It's not that serious.

22:20.740 --> 22:22.360
Of course it's serious.

22:23.240 --> 22:24.360
Does it hurt?

22:26.910 --> 22:31.120
You might not remember this,
but you went through a lot last night.

22:31.580 --> 22:35.879
We had Dr. Nagakura make a house call,
and he gave you an IV.

22:35.880 --> 22:38.669
I never want to have
to go through that again.

22:38.670 --> 22:40.380
It won't happen again.

22:40.800 --> 22:42.169
Don't worry.

22:42.170 --> 22:44.890
There's no way this will happen again.

23:00.030 --> 23:03.239
<i>Your collar is unbuttoned.</i>

23:03.240 --> 23:04.830
<i>What's your name and class?</i>

23:08.700 --> 23:12.000
<i>Why is your attitude so awful, you fool?!</i>

23:12.330 --> 23:14.379
<i>It's because you're being unreasonable.</i>

23:14.380 --> 23:16.300
<i>How am I being unreasonable?</i>

23:20.880 --> 23:23.050
<i>It doesn't make sense at all.</i>

23:23.090 --> 23:25.555
Episode 3: "Dispute"
